# Copy to /etc/hoanglong-bo/staging.env on the VPS, root:root 0600. NEVER committed.
#
# Outside the git tree on purpose, and named explicitly by every compose command
# (`--env-file /etc/hoanglong-bo/staging.env`). The old instruction pointed at
# /opt/hoanglong-bo/.env, which compose never read: it looks beside the compose
# file, one directory further down, and does not walk upwards.
#
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD="$(openssl rand -hex 24)"
#
# HEX, NOT BASE64, and not for looks. This value is interpolated into
# DATABASE_URL as postgres://user:PASSWORD@host/db, and base64's alphabet
# includes "/", which ends the userinfo component and makes the URL
# unparseable. Measured: 39.7% of `openssl rand -base64 24` outputs contain one.
# Hex is 24 bytes either way - 192 bits - just spelled in an alphabet a URI
# cannot misread.
#
# Nothing here reaches the frontend bundle: the client is served as static files
# and talks to /api on its own origin.
POSTGRES_USER=backoffice
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=backoffice
LOG_LEVEL=log
# The docker bridge nginx's upstream arrives from. Widen only with a measured
# reason — see TRUSTED_PROXIES in backend/src/config/env.schema.ts.
TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.16.0.0/12
